  "html": "<!DOCTYPE html><html><head><title>Great Victorian Rail Trail – Rail Trails Australia</title></head><body><h2>Great Victorian Rail Trail</h2><div><span class=\"statIcn\">Location:</span><span>90km north of Melbourne</span></div><div><span class=\"statIcn\">Length:</span><span>135 km</span></div><div><span class=\"statIcn\">Surface:</span><span>Compacted earth, Fine gravel</span></div><div><span class=\"statIcn\">Start / End:</span><span>Tallarook to Alexandra and Mansfield</span></div><div class=\"custDtlRtCont\"><p>One of Victoria's longest rail trails at 134km, the Great Victorian traverses undulating farmland from the Goulburn River at Tallarook and Yea up to the High Country.</p><p>The central section has been affected by bushfires. Some sections are closed until further notice.</p></div></body></html>",
